  "estudio": "Por si acaso, para colmo",
  "alumno": "Just in case, to top it all"
 },
 "intro": "Por and para at B2: the contrasts that change the meaning, and the fixed phrases.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "por si acaso",
   "significado": "just in case",
   "pron": "por si a-KA-so",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is written as three words and used on its own: «llévate el paraguas, por si acaso».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por fin",
   "significado": "at last",
   "pron": "por fin",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It expresses relief after a wait: «¡por fin llegas!».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por poco",
   "significado": "nearly, almost",
   "pron": "por PO-ko",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with the present for something that almost happened: «por poco me caigo» (I did not fall).",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "para colmo",
   "significado": "to top it all",
   "pron": "PA-ra KOL-mo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It adds a final problem: «y, para colmo, llovía». «El colmo» is the limit.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "para variar",
   "significado": "for a change (often ironic)",
   "pron": "PA-ra ba-RYAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is often ironic: «llegó tarde, para variar». It means it is the usual thing.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por mí",
   "significado": "as far as I'm concerned",
   "pron": "por MI",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Por mí, vale» means «I don't mind». Here «mí» has an accent.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "para mí",
   "significado": "in my opinion; for me",
   "pron": "PA-ra MI",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Para mí, es un error» gives an opinion. It can also be «es para mí», a gift.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "no es para tanto",
   "significado": "it's not such a big deal",
   "pron": "no es PA-ra TAN-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It plays something down: «no es para tanto». You say it to someone who exaggerates.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
