   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Where they part",
     "texto": [
      "**Por** looks at what lies behind: the cause (por amor), the doer (escrito **por**), the exchange (lo compré **por** diez euros), on someone's behalf (hazlo **por** mí), the way through (**por** el parque), rough time and place (**por** la mañana, **por** aquí), the means (**por** correo), the rate (dos veces **por** semana), and what is still to do (queda mucho **por** hacer).\n\n**Para** looks ahead: the purpose, the receiver, the direction (salgo **para** Madrid), the deadline (**para** el lunes), an opinion (**para mí**), an employer (trabajo **para** un banco), and a comparison with what you would expect: **para ser** extranjero, habla muy bien.\n\nMinimal pairs: lo hice **por ti** (because of you) and lo hice **para ti** (to give to you). **Por mí**, vale (I don't mind) and **para mí**, es un error (in my view).\n\n**Estar para** is to be about to, or in the mood for: no estoy **para** bromas. **Estar por** is to be inclined to, or still to be done."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Pairs that change the meaning",
     "texto": [
      "- lo hice **por** ti (because of you) / lo hice **para** ti (to give to you)\n- gracias **por** venir / estudio **para** aprender\n- pasé **por** Madrid (through) / salgo **para** Madrid (towards)\n- lo compré **por** diez euros / es **para** el lunes\n- **por** mí, vale (I don't mind) / **para** mí, es un error (in my view)"
     ],
